{"id": "tech-3", "headline": "FAA probes Amazon drone that crashed onto a garage", "source": "Ars Technica", "url": "https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/faa-opens-probe-after-amazon-delivery-drone-clips-cable-crashes-into-garage/", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["The Federal Aviation Administration is investigating after an Amazon delivery drone clipped a fiber-optic line and crashed onto a garage roof in Huntington Woods, Michigan, on November 20. Residents Jim Brennan and his wife had ordered shampoo and were told it would arrive by drone in seven minutes. After the drone dropped the package in their backyard, it lost a propeller on the cable and ended up pinned between a neighbor's garage roof and power lines. The FAA's preliminary notice says the aircraft struck a fiber cable and a garage and became entangled in power lines during takeoff. Amazon's MK30 drones carry up to five pounds and have obstacle avoidance.", "The incident comes as Amazon and others expand drone delivery across the US. Source: Ars Technica."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110010011101101101111001111101111111", "10000010100001110100001000111000101000001", "10111010001101001001110010101011001011101", "10111010111110111011001011110100001011101", "10111010010100010011011100000011101011101", "10000010100010111110110000111010101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000001110010000111010111001000000000", "11111011111001110110000101110110010101010", "01100001000010001011110110101111101111011", "01111011000100011010111001010010101000000", "10001000001110110010110100111000000011010", "01101011001010010010001111110101000001100", "00111001100000111111100100101101111011001", "10100111111110100000101000110100110111000", "11010001100100101001111000011010101001010", "00111010100111100100001111100101000100100", "10101101101101101101100110101011101110011", "10111111001011111100001011011010000110000", "11110101111111011110011100010011110011000", "0001011